     "explanation": "Manson argues that unlimited choice taxes every moment with the ghosts of foregone options and keeps experience shallow. Committing deeply closes those doors, ending the second-guessing and freeing your energy for one path. That constraint grants access to rewards — mastery, intimacy, meaning — that only accumulate on the far side of sustained commitment. Freedom is not an open menu; it is being free enough to choose and stay.",
